  note    five layouts: the fraction as needed (Go's `RFC3339Nano`), none (`RFC3339`), and 3, 6 or 9 digits always, cut toward the past; `Z` always, where Python writes `+00:00`. Go's `String` adds a zone name, and the debug text is this one here

capability text/rfc3339-read  an instant read from RFC 3339
  heroes  time.parse
  go      time.Parse (RFC3339), Time.UnmarshalText, Time.UnmarshalJSON, time.ParseError, ParseError.Error
  rust    -
  python  datetime.datetime.fromisoformat, datetime.date.fromisoformat, datetime.time.fromisoformat
  note    read exactly: `T` or `t` and `Z` or `z` as RFC 3339 allows (Go refuses the lower case), a fraction of any length cut after nine digits (as Go), an offset moved to UTC and one past 23:59 refused (Go accepts `+24:00`); a space for the `T` is refused, which Python reads. A failure is `invalid` with its byte in the message, Go's `ParseError`; an instant past the range is `does_not_fit`, where Go wraps

