capability retry/backoff  the waits of a retry loop: exponential from a first wait, capped, spread by chance
  heroes  time.backoff, time.Backoff, time.Jitter, time.with_jitter, time.wait_after
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    no standard library of the three has one. The yardsticks are PyPI's tenacity (its exponential waits, a multiplier and a cap, and random ones), Go's cenkalti/backoff (`ExponentialBackOff`: an initial interval, a multiplier, a largest interval, a randomization factor) and Polly; none is on this machine (tenacity absent from Python 3.15's site, cenkalti/backoff's module cache holding no source to build, 2026-11-17), so no answer of theirs was observed. The wait after the n-th failure is `first` times `multiplier` to the n-1 (tenacity's), capped at `longest`; the jitters are AWS's Architecture Blog's, "Exponential Backoff And Jitter": full, equal and decorrelated, the last between `first` and the previous wait times the policy's multiplier where AWS writes 3; `spread` is cenkalti's randomization factor, capped at `longest` where cenkalti lets a randomized wait pass its largest interval. The program draws the fraction, `random.next_f64`, so `time` carries no generator; the growth is in floats, exact below 2^53 nanoseconds, checked against Python's float arithmetic

capability retry/limits  a retry loop that gives up after a count of attempts or a total time
  heroes  time.Retry, time.new_retry, time.next_wait, time.with_attempts, time.with_total, time.LIMIT, time.TIMEOUT
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    tenacity's stop after a count of attempts or a delay and cenkalti's `MaxElapsedTime` are the yardsticks; the total is judged as cenkalti documents it, the time spent plus the next wait against it, and the end of the attempts fails `limit`, the end of the time `timeout`. The program loops, sleeps and calls; tenacity's decorator and cenkalti's `Retry` call a closure, which Heroes has not

