capability schedule/cron-read  a cron expression read: five fields or six, names, lists, ranges, steps, `L`, `W`, `#` and the descriptors
  heroes  time.parse_cron, time.Cron
  go      -
  rust    -
  python  -
  note    no standard library of the three reads cron. The yardstick is Go's robfig/cron v3, run on this machine at v3.0.1 on 2026-11-17: its five fields, its six with the seconds first (`WithSeconds`), its names of three letters in any case, its descriptors in lower case only, its `?` as `*`, and its day fields joined by OR where both are restricted and by AND where either holds a `*` or `?` with no step above 1 (so `*/10` restricts, where Vixie cron reads every field opening with `*` as open). Beyond robfig, which refuses them: Sunday as 7 and a range's end at Sunday (`FRI-SUN`, `6-0`) as Vixie cron reads them, a step from a value or `*` in the day of the week ending at Saturday; Quartz's `L`, `L-n`, `nW`, `LW`, `nL` and `n#k`, in lists too, judged against Python's `calendar`. Refused where robfig accepts: an empty item (`1,,2`), `@every` under a second or not whole seconds (robfig rounds them), `CRON_TZ=` (the zone is the search's argument); `@reboot` and Quartz's seventh field, the year, are refused as robfig refuses them

