  note    every instant whose local time on the zone's clocks the schedule allows, as robfig/cron answers: a time a change of offset skipped never runs, one it repeated runs at both its instants; `@every` runs that long after the whole second, as robfig. 1,400 random expressions, from instants between 2024 and 2028 over eight zones (UTC, Rome, London, New York, Sao Paulo, Tehran, Chatham and Lord Howe), answered five runs each as robfig did but one: robfig skips 2026-04-05 19:13:27 in Lord Howe, a local time that exists once after its half-hour change (Python's `zoneinfo` agrees), and this search does not. The search ends at the last instant an `Instant` holds, in 2262, a schedule that never runs failing `not_found` there, where robfig gives up five years on

